# Sample corpus (SPEC 8.3a). The raw reports and photographs are somebody's real
# vehicles, photographed in somebody's garage, so they stay on the machine that made
# them. What ships is redacted word geometry plus its fixtures - see
# homeautoshop/scantools/capture.py. Note the directory itself is NOT ignored:
# a negation cannot re-include anything inside an excluded directory.
# Parts orders are shipping documents: a name, a street address, a phone number and an
# email, twice over. Captured as redacted text and geometry by
# homeautoshop/purchasing/importers/capture.py, and the capture is what ships.
Artifacts/samples/**/*.pdf
# `**/`, not `*/`. This one read `Artifacts/samples/*.jpg` while its three
# neighbours matched at any depth, so photographs one folder further down -
# `scan-reports/bt600plus/*.jpg`, tool screens shot in the garage - were not
# ignored at all and a `git add -A` would have taken them.
Artifacts/samples/**/*.jpg
Artifacts/samples/**/*.jpeg
Artifacts/samples/**/*.png
Artifacts/samples/**/*.cfa
Artifacts/samples/backups/

# Research notes for a later phase: manifests of third-party scan reports found
# on the public web, kept for their formats. Not ours to republish, and some of
# the URLs carry the VIN of the vehicle the report was made for - so redacting
# would break the link the entry exists for, and keeping it would put somebody's
# VIN in a public repository. It stays on the machine that gathered it.
Artifacts/samples/**/automotive_scan_tool_public_examples*.json

# Samples fetched from the public web by `manage.py fetch_scan_samples`. Other
# people's reports, published to be read rather than for us to redistribute,
# and several carry a VIN. Ignored as a whole directory rather than by
# extension: the operator's own reports are a PDF from a scan tool or a JPEG
# from a phone, so a list of extensions covers them, but a file off the public
# web has whatever extension its publisher felt like and one unanticipated
# `.dat` would be in a public repository forever. What ships is the redacted
# capture beside it and the provenance in sources.json.
Artifacts/samples/**/originals/

# Published trouble-code lists, transcribed by `manage.py build_dtc_list` into
# homeautoshop/diagnostics/codelists/. Somebody else's manual or web page, kept
# so a committed table can be checked against what it came from. Ignored as a
# whole directory for the same reason `originals/` is: these arrive as a PDF,
# a saved web page or a text dump, and an extension list is a rule that has to
# be remembered. What ships is the transcription, which names its source.
Artifacts/samples/dtc-lists/
